# NeoBench program entry.
#
# The first line of a file that is neither blank nor a comment may say
# what the file is for.  "program = name" makes the file an entry rather
# than a document: choosing it in Files starts that program instead of
# opening it, so a drawer can hold a program the way the start menu
# does.  The name is one of the desktop's own -- files, clock, monitor,
# about, preferences, neotext, vlc -- and a file that names anything
# else, or that says nothing at all, opens in the reader as it always
# has.
#
# VLC is filed here, in the drawer that holds the media, because that
# is the drawer it plays: the pictures, the films and the sounds are
# the files it reads, so the entry stands beside them rather than in
# the tools.  It is the one program of the seven that has to look at
# the store before it can show anything at all, and it lists what it
# finds -- the still pictures in Pictures, the films in Videos, the
# sounds in Music, and whatever of the three is filed here with it.
#
# The start menu lists it as well, under the rule beside Preferences:
# the menu keeps the programs the machine is for, and a player for the
# media drawer is one of them.  This file is the way to it from where
# the media itself is.

program = vlc
